      "target": "../sections/page-007.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 4\n\n3.1 Process of Behavioural Change : A Continuum\n\nBringing about a behavioural change is, however, a difficult process. The task is further\ncomplicated by the sensitive and personal nature of the issues, dealing as they largely do with\nsex and sexuality. A variety of approaches and messages will be needed to promote movement\nof individuals and populations along the continuum of behavioural change. The \"adoption of\nsafer sex\" example below illustrates the various stages of the behavioural change model shown\nin Figure 2.\n\nFigure 2. Behavioural change model\n\nUnaware\n+\nAware\nv\nC",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces a behavioural change model with stages from unaware to adopting new behaviour, illustrated with safer sex, and notes how awareness can be raised among different groups.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-205344/blocks/prose-page-008",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 8",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/page-008.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 5\n\nConcerned\n\nIt is possible to be aware without being concerned. Information must be given is such\na way that the audience feels it applies to them, i.e., the audience becomes concerned, and\npeople are motivated to evaluate their own behaviour.\n\nMass media approaches aimed at the general population are less likely to be\neffective in creating concern and overcoming denial, particularly among those at\ngreatest risk. Targeted communication and interpersonal approaches are therefore\nmore useful.\n\nKnowledgeable and Skilled\n\nOnce concerned, individuals may acquire more knowledge by",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the middle stages of the behaviour change continuum: becoming concerned, gaining knowledge and skills, and trying new behaviour. It stresses that targeted and interpersonal approaches work better than mass media for creating concern, and that condom negotiation and use skills are essential.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-205344/blocks/prose-page-009",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 9",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/page-009.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 6\n\nAdoption of New Behaviour\n\nFinally, the individual decides to remain faithful to one faithful partner or regularly uses\ncondoms as a source of protection from AIDS/STD.\n\nAssuming the new behaviour continues to be evaluated as largely positive,\nsustained behavioural change could take place at this stage. Continuous messages\nof support and access to condoms are still essential.\n\nProgrammes must ensure that overall and individual stages of behavioural change are\ntaken into consideration when IEC approaches and activities are being planned and\nimplemented.\n\n3.2 The Role of IEC",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Covers the final stage of adopting and sustaining new behaviour, then sets out roles of IEC in STD and AIDS prevention. These include informing and motivating at-risk groups, reaching intermediaries and reducing stigma and discrimination against people with HIV.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
