      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 10",
      "pageStart": 10,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/page-010.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 7\n\n(3) Support for various components of an AIDS Prevention and Control\nProgramme: IEC campaigns can promote seeking of quality STD services,\nwhich of course must be made available. IEC can also support efforts to\npromote voluntary blood donation and the implementation of universal\nprecautions in health care settings.\n\n4. LESSONS LEARNT FROM IEC PROGRAMME EXPERIENCES\n\nCountries in South-East Asia can benefit from the experiences gained within as well as\noutside the Region. Learning from others allows programme managers to initiate more\neffective strategies and communication ap",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Notes IEC support for STD services, voluntary blood donation and universal precautions, then begins a section on lessons from IEC experience. It warns that campaigns blaming particular groups such as sex workers and drug users can be counterproductive.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
