      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 14\n\n5.2. Preparatory Activities\n\nEssential preparatory activities include developing linkages, establishing coordination\nfor essential services and ensuring availability of trained manpower.\n\n5.2.1 Develop linkages\n\nLinkages for implementation of IEC activities within the government may be with the\nministries of education, youth, women and child welfare, tourism, information and\nbroadcasting, and transportation. Integration with MCH/FP programmes is an important\nstrategy to reach women and should be a major priority. Collaboration with various ministries\nis also needed for adv",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes preparatory activities for IEC programmes, including linkages with ministries such as education, youth and tourism and integration with maternal and child health and family planning services. It also covers coordinating essential services and training key categories of workers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
