        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 18",
      "pageStart": 18,
      "pageEnd": 18,
      "target": "../sections/page-018.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 15\n\n— NGO workers/volunteers, and\n— Leaders or peers from high-risk populations and vulnerable groups.\n\n5.3. Materials Development\n\nSuitable partners should be identified to assist in materials development. This is\nespecially important if ministries of health do not have the in-house capacity for development\nof IEC materials appropriate to meeting the needs of the programme. As a general strategy,\nit is suggested that the actual development of materials be contracted out to appropriate\nprofessionals, if available. The demands of targeting materials to produce sexual behaviour",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists further groups needing training and moves on to materials development, recommending that ministries contract suitable professionals where in-house capacity is lacking. It discusses formative research and choosing messages, media and channels for each target group.",
