      "pageEnd": 21,
      "target": "../sections/page-021.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 18\n\nnever reach those who need them or who could most effectively use them. Planning a\ndistribution strategy and setting up a distribution network at the beginning is important.\n\nUsing materials to support IEC activities, through mass media or for interpersonal\ncommunication requires knowing how to use them effectively. Ideally, users will become\nfamiliar with different types of materials and methods for using them during communication\ntraining. At the very least, instructions and suggestions for use must be supplied along with\nthe materials.\n\n5.4 Monitoring and Evaluation\n\nMo",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Discusses distribution networks and training users in how to use IEC materials, then begins the monitoring and evaluation section. It distinguishes monitoring of inputs and performance against standards, with examples such as training health workers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
