    {
      "id": "library/10665-205344/blocks/prose-page-024",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 24",
      "pageStart": 24,
      "pageEnd": 24,
      "target": "../sections/page-024.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 21\n\nSome evaluation methods are outlined below:\n\nCommunity surveys, such as the general population survey: These are usually regionally\n(and sometimes nationally) focused investigations. They can be conducted as household\nsurveys, which collect information from a representative sample of a population and are\nconducted by trained interviewers who go to the dwellings in a selected geographic area for\nface-to-face interviews, or targeted population surveys, which collect information about a\npopulation of particular interest, and are carried out in locations where these population",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Outlines evaluation methods such as household and targeted population surveys and comprehensive programme reviews of national AIDS plans and IEC policies. The page closes by naming the experts from India, Sri Lanka, Thailand and WHO/SEARO who took part in preparing the document.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
