    {
      "id": "library/10665-205344/blocks/prose-page-028",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 28",
      "pageStart": 28,
      "pageEnd": 28,
      "target": "../sections/page-028.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEA/AIDS/81\nPage 25\n\n— Reduce the number of sexual partners;\n\n— Increase condom use;\n\n— Discuss sexual matters openly;\n\n— Actively seek information on sexual matters and seek counselling;\n— Seek STD services; and\n\n— Develop ‘enabling skills’ to promote healthy lifestyles.\n\nIn the Region as a whole, these would be the primary goals, since almost all the HIV\ninfection is sexually transmitted. However, in certain parts of some countries (e.g. India,\nThailand, Myanmar), injecting drug use is also a major problem. In such areas, the\nbehavioural goals will have to emphasize sterilization and non-sha",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Completes the list of behavioural goals for youth, including fewer partners, condom use and seeking STD services, and notes that injecting drug use calls for needle-related goals in parts of India, Thailand and Myanmar. It also stresses measurable objectives and partnerships with other programmes, such as STD and family planning services.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
